# Everything else: see .env.advanced.example — you almost certainly don't need it.
#
# MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL on four CMP 170HX cards. ./start.sh copies this file to .env
# on first run and reads only .env. Every setting is commented out and shows its
# default; uncomment a line to change it, then run ./start.sh restart.
# One KEY=value per line; a value on the command line beats .env for that run:
#   CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,2,3,4 ./start.sh restart
# The four cards to serve on, as nvidia-smi numbers them (exactly four, distinct).
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3
# Listen address: 127.0.0.1 = this machine only; 0.0.0.0 = every interface (set API_KEY first).
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# API port.
# PORT=8000
# When set, every /v1 request must send "Authorization: Bearer <key>"; unset = no key.
# API_KEY=
# The model id clients send.
# SERVED_MODEL_NAME=mimo-v2.6-flash
# Where the checkpoint goes, as an absolute path (~183 GiB). Default: models/ in this repo.
# MODELS_DIR=/path/to/models
# Speculative decoding: dflash (MiMo's own DFlash drafter, the default), mtp (the
# head inside the checkpoint) or none. See the README for which suits what.
# SPEC_MODE=dflash
# Peer access: auto verifies content before enabling P2P.
# off disables it; force bypasses verification.
# P2P=auto
